<header><p class="enc-kicker">State</p><h1 class="enc-title">Weimar Republic</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as German Republic</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/weimar">Weimar</a> Republic was the democratic German state established after the fall of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/german-empire">German Empire</a> in 1918, named after the city where its constitution was drafted. It faced the burdens of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/treaty-of-versailles">Treaty of Versailles</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/war-reparations">reparations</a>, hyperinflation and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/great-depression">Great Depression</a>. Accounts of the German Empire place it as the immediate successor to the empire; it ended with the Nazi seizure of power in 1933.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/weimar-republic.jpg" alt="Weimar Republic" width="320" height="214" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Mmxx · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Flag_of_Germany_(3-2).svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
